WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.010
In 2018, more than 108,000 people

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:07.350
finished ultramarathons in the US alone.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.900
An ultramarathon is any race
longer than 42 kilometers,

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.940
and races can range anywhere from 50

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.583
to over 4,000 kilometers.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.570
But one of the more common lengths

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.840
covers about 100 kilometers

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.800
and takes on average 17 hours to finish.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.140
In some of the longer races,

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.490
half the runners never
see the finish line,

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.980
and that's because these
races not only push you

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.150
to your mental limit, they
take a toll on your body

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.083
both inside and out.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.000
Ultrarunners endure some
pretty extreme conditions.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.400
The Badwater Ultramarathon, for example,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.920
covers 4,000 meters of
elevation through Death Valley

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.510
in July, one of the
hottest months of the year.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:01.990
Temperatures can reach
up to 47 degrees Celsius,

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.230
causing headaches and
dizziness in many runners.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.880
But even if you're running
in more comfortable weather,

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.930
you could still be feeling
sick to your stomach.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.080
One of the most common
issues in any ultramarathon

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.870
is nausea or vomiting.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.460
It affects about 37% of
people who complete a race,

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.250
but it's also the No. 1 reason

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.130
runners won't finish in the first place.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.690
That's because running
disrupts your digestion.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.880
It diverts blood away from
your stomach to your muscles,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.940
and since ultramarathons last so long,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.290
many races provide sandwiches, pasta,

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.460
and other carb-loaded meals.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.551
But as a result, that
food will just sit around

00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:43.090
undigested causing a lot of problems.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.410
But if your stomach
isn't slowing you down,

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.020
your eyes could be causing you grief.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.030
Windy conditions can dry
out or damage the cells

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.110
that pump a protective liquid layer

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.900
over your cornea, which
can cause it to swell up

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.820
and blur your vision.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.430
During the Hellgate 100K, for example,

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.870
runners report losing most of their vision

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.040
by the end of the race.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.550
They call it Hellgate Eyes.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.020
But no amount of protection or preparation

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.910
can prevent one symptom:
That's sleepiness.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:17.370
For a 17-hour race, it
might not be so bad,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.890
but longer races can stretch
for more than 24 hours,

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.720
which can make sleepy runners
more prone to trips and falls

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.910
or worse: hallucinations.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.730
The Barkley Marathons, for example,

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.120
is a race where runners are given 60 hours

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.620
to finish 161 kilometers.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.850
In 2005, one runner reported
that he thought he saw houses

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.100
at the top of the mountain

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.340
and believed he was their garbage man

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.840
sent to pick up their trash.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.610
Despite these health hazards,

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.950
ultrarunning is a growing
sport, believe it or not.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:53.170
One study found that
compared to marathoners,

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.720
ultrarunners are more
likely to do it for nature

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.210
and a sense of purpose than
for the competitive aspect.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.670
So if you're up for the challenge,

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:04.500
plenty of races are on
trails through natural areas.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.440
So at least you'll get a great view.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.490
You might be hallucinating

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.440
that you're someone's garbage
man, but it will look pretty.

